{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ECCkRVhS8wPVXqySRxVcRS","type":"tool_result","content":"97:- [ ] **13 Assemble.** Finish `paper2/equivalences.md` as section 3 of the\n98-  paper: the master table (every problem, source, relation, Lean name,\n99-  status: proved / sandwich / monotone only / stated gap / false as stated),\n100-  a figure-ready diagram of the equivalence chain as a Mermaid or DOT graph,\n101-  and a list of every allowed sorry with its reason. Write\n102-  `paper2/lean_repo_plan.md`: which files move to the paper's own Lean\n103-  repository, their dependency order, and what of the existing\n104-  `lean/MOSPFormalization/` they need.\n105-\n106-- [ ] **14 Reserve.** The best remaining gap: attempt the full node search\n107-  theorem (monotonicity, Kirousis & Papadimitriou 1986 / Bienstock &\n108-  Seymour) or LaPaugh's theorem, whichever item 10-11 left closer. One\n109-  session; if it does not close, record how far it got and stop.\n# One line per sorry this loop is allowed to leave, beyond the baseline one in\n# Sandwich.lean (the §24 conjecture). Format: file | theorem | why it is a\n# stated gap and not a hard proof abandoned. Only phase-3 items (10-12, 14) may\n# add lines, and each line must also appear in paper2/equivalences.md.\n 1153 paper2/equivalences.md\n  175 paper2/plan.md\n 1328 total\nlean/MOSPFormalization/Complex:\nEdgeSearch.lean\nEdgeSeparation.lean\nGateMatrix.lean\nIntervalSearch.lean\nIntervalThickness.lean\nKirousisPapadimitriouGap.lean\nNarrowness.lean\nNodeSearch.lean\nOneDimLogic.lean\nPLAFolding.lean\nSplitBandwidth.lean\n\npaper2:\nREADME.md\n__pycache__\ncitation_graph.py\ncomplex_check.py\ndata\nequivalences.md\nfigures\nliterature\nplan.md\npopularity.md\nproof_reductions.md\nrelevance.py\ntable1.bib\ntrends.py\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Regression gate for loop0005 (the pathwidth complex in Lean).\n\nPasses only if all four hold:\n1. `lake build` in lean/ succeeds;\n2. every file under lean/MOSPFormalization/Complex/ is imported by\n   lean/MOSPFormalization.lean, so the build really checks it;\n3. the number of `sorry` in Lean *code* (comments and docstrings stripped) is\n   at most the baseline (1: the §24 conjecture in Sandwich.lean) plus the\n   entries in allowed_sorries.txt, and no `axiom` declaration exists outside\n   the baseline;\n4. `python -m pytest tests/ -q -x` passes.\n\n    python3 Ralph_Loops/loop0005/gate.py\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nREPO = HERE.parents[1]\nLEAN = REPO / \"lean\"\nBASELINE_SORRIES = 1\nALLOWED = HERE / \"allowed_sorries.txt\"\n\n\ndef strip_comments(src: str) -> str:\n    out, i, depth = [], 0, 0\n    while i < len(src):\n        if src.startswith(\"/-\", i):\n            depth += 1; i += 2; continue\n        if depth and src.startswith(\"-/\", i):\n            depth -= 1; i += 2; continue\n        if depth:\n            i += 1; continue\n        if src.startswith(\"--\", i):\n            j = src.find(\"\\n\", i); i = len(src) if j < 0 else j; continue\n        if src[i] == '\"':\n            j = i + 1\n            while j < len(src) and src[j] != '\"':\n                j += 2 if src[j] == \"\\\\\" else 1\n            i = j + 1; continue\n        out.append(src[i]); i += 1\n    return \"\".join(out)\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    ok = True\n    b = subprocess.run([\"lake\", \"build\"], cwd=LEAN, capture_output=True, text=True)\n    tail = \"\\n\".join((b.stdout + b.stderr).splitlines()[-25:])\n    if b.returncode != 0:\n        print(\"GATE FAIL: lake build\\n\" + tail); return 1\n    print(\"lake build: ok\")\n\n    root = (LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization.lean\").read_text()\n    for f in sorted((LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization\" / \"Complex\").rglob(\"*.lean\")):\n        mod = \"MOSPFormalization.\" + \".\".join(f.relative_to(LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization\").with_suffix(\"\").parts)\n        if f\"import {mod}\" not in root:\n            print(f\"GATE FAIL: {mod} is not imported by MOSPFormalization.lean\"); ok = False\n\n    sorries, axioms = [], []\n    for f in sorted((LEAN / \"MOSPFormalization\").rglob(\"*.lean\")):\n        code = strip_comments(f.read_text())\n        for n, line in enumerate(code.splitlines(), 1):\n            if re.search(r\"\\bsorry\\b\", line):\n                sorries.append(f\"{f.relative_to(LEAN)}:{n}\")\n            if re.match(r\"\\s*(private\\s+)?axiom\\b\", line):\n                axioms.append(f\"{f.relative_to(LEAN)}:{n}\")\n    allowed = [l for l in ALLOWED.read_text().splitlines() if l.strip() and not l.startswith(\"#\")] if ALLOWED.exists() else []\n    limit = BASELINE_SORRIES + len(allowed)\n    print(f\"sorry in code: {len(sorries)} (limit {limit}): {sorries}\")\n    if len(sorries) > limit:\n        print(\"GATE FAIL: more sorry than the baseline plus allowed_sorries.txt\"); ok = False\n    if axioms:\n        print(f\"GATE FAIL: axiom declarations: {axioms}\"); ok = False\n\n    t = subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pytest\", \"tests/\", \"-q\", \"-x\"], cwd=REPO,","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"747dc9e7-b51a-40c7-bf22-0f086073294d","uuid":"0df77645-16d8-470c-8994-989e5c1271c0","timestamp":"2026-09-30T13:47:32.378Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"97:- [ ] **13 Assemble.** Finish `paper2/equivalences.md` as section 3 of the\n98-  paper: the master table (every problem, source, relation, Lean name,\n99-  status: proved / sandwich / monotone only / stated gap / false as stated),\n100-  a figure-ready diagram of the equivalence chain as a Mermaid or DOT graph,\n101-  and a list of every allowed sorry with its reason. Write\n102-  `paper2/lean_repo_plan.md`: which files move to the paper's own Lean\n103-  repository, their dependency order, and what of the existing\n104-  `lean/MOSPFormalization/` they need.\n105-\n106-- [ ] **14 Reserve.** The best remaining gap: attem